{page==='about'&&<><section className="author-hero"><div className="author-mark">D</div><div><div className="eyebrow">CREATOR · PRODUCT DESIGNER · SOFTWARE AUTHOR</div><h2>Dinesh</h2><p>Dinesh created Identity API Lab to make complex enterprise identity work easier to understand, test and demonstrate. The project brings provisioning, authentication, authorization, audit evidence and a permission-aware business portal into one connected local experience.</p><a className="primary linkedin-button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dineshwarmanukonda/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><Linkedin size={17}/>Connect with Dinesh<ArrowUpRight size={16}/></a></div></section><div className="three-card-grid"><section className="card author-value"><Fingerprint size={23}/><h3>Identity made visible</h3><p>One canonical identity state is exercised through REST, SOAP, SCIM 2.0 and GraphQL so developers can see how each integration affects the same employee lifecycle.</p></section><section className="card author-value"><ShieldCheck size={23}/><h3>Security with evidence</h3><p>Scoped credentials, operation permissions, object checks, revocation and correlated audit history turn security decisions into something teams can inspect.</p></section><section className="card author-value"><Sparkles size={23}/><h3>Built for exploration</h3><p>A polished command center, authentication studio, request explorer and banking workspace make serious integration testing approachable and useful.</p></section></div><section className="card author-story"><div><div className="eyebrow">THE WORK BEHIND THE PRODUCT</div><h2>From protocol test to complete journey</h2></div><div className="author-principles"><div><b>Connected by design</b><span>Identity, APIs, permissions and the portal share one source of truth.</span></div><div><b>Honest capability</b><span>Working features are separated clearly from integrations that need external infrastructure.</span></div><div><b>Practical learning</b><span>Every action can be tested, observed and traced through the local environment.</span></div><div><b>Made by Dinesh</b><span>Authorship is recorded in the product, source metadata, project notice and documentation.</span></div></div></section></>}
